  "id": "Compound::DB06218 - Gene::768",
  "verbalization": "Lacosamide is proposed to interact with Ca9 through a series of mechanistic steps involving the binding of Lacosamide to calcium-binding sites on Ca5b, Ca6, and Ca3. These interactions are supported by the evidence that Lacosamide binds to calcium-containing proteins, which then participate in the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide or carbonate dehydratase activity. These processes are ultimately linked to Ca9, suggesting that Lacosamide may influence cellular functions associated with calcium homeostasis or metabolic pathways. The cumulative evidence from the three paths indicates a potential role for Lacosamide in modulating calcium-related processes in Ca9, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of Lacosamide in the biological processes of Ca9.",
